# PROVENANCE — INFINITY6C / 0907 / glibc 11.1.0 and uclibc 9.1.0

SigmaStar Alkaid SDK for Infinity6C (vendor CHIP = i6c), the SSC377 line.
Prebuilt userspace MI libraries. Nothing here is built from source.

## Release

    release_0907   built 2022-09-07
    project_commit 3a7aec9
    sdk_commit     3dcd67a
    mhal_commit    a7acd5c

Both variants come from the same drop and carry the same three commits. Their
build stamps are minutes apart:

    glibc  11.1.0   build_time.20220907112126
    uclibc  9.1.0   build_time.20220907111141

Read the stamp out of any file with:

    strings libmi_sys.so | grep 'Sigmastar Module'

## Origin

Taken from the vendor SDK release tree, not harvested from a shipped firmware
and not taken from OpenIPC. This is a stronger provenance than the INFINITY6E
entry beside it, which was reconstructed from a camera image.

    ssc377/release_0907/sourcecode/project/release/chip/i6c/ipc/common/
      glibc/11.1.0/mi_libs/dynamic/
      uclibc/9.1.0/mi_libs/dynamic/

OpenIPC's sigmastar-osdrv-infinity6c ships the same drop -- identical
project/sdk/mhal commits -- but only the uclibc 9.1.0 variant, and 20 of its
31 libraries. It is a subset of what is here, so nothing was taken from it.

## The two variants are not interchangeable

They differ in content, not only in codegen. glibc carries two libraries uclibc
does not:

    libmi_divp.so
    libsigma3a.so

so the C library component of the path is load-bearing, and a build that picks
the wrong one is missing libraries rather than getting differently compiled
ones.

    glibc  11.1.0   32 libraries
    uclibc  9.1.0   31 libraries

    md5 libmi_sys.so  glibc   f7ff32117b58c0f29f2c0b7533306c78
    md5 libmi_sys.so  uclibc  0c3e8b543918b509ddaa1b1f8b5ee2ac

## Unstamped

    libsigma3a.so

carries no vendor build stamp, so its drop cannot be confirmed from the binary
and is asserted only by the tree it was copied out of. It is glibc-only.

## Not consumed yet

No thingino target builds Infinity6C. This family runs a 5.10.61 kernel while
the SigmaStar port is 4.9.84 throughout, so these libraries are staged for a
port that does not exist rather than supporting one that does. Nothing here has
been loaded on hardware.

No source is available and none is claimed here.
